{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact NF-4 head 1904c9458a3414dc1998cab6bb72ad3912f6a94b on builder/cli-install-nf4-20261112, all 31 artifacts, for request d2aff067 under promise c67cd117 and review request cc7e3fc6. The head does what d2aff067 asks, in the shape that rulings 19a509a5 and f4f50949 set. `dap install` and `dap application` call the client and load no MCP module. MCP's two tools call the same client functions and return the same bytes as before.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `packages/client/src/install-request.ts` holds the logic of MCP's old `#applicationRoom`, `#installApplication` and `#applicationInstallation`, in the same order:\n  1. the key check;\n  2. the room and sibling checks;\n  3. the `admit` hook;\n  4. the option parse;\n  5. the trust check before custody and again inside the build;\n  6. the publisher check;\n  7. the Commons check;\n  8. signing;\n  9. the custody send;\n  10. the receipt check;\n  11. the entry read and the entry check.\n- Each `stopCall` of the old code becomes a typed refusal. Errors inside the build cross custody as `Refused` and become the same refusals. The record-phase test that tells `stopped` from `unprepared` is unchanged.\n- `declarationDigest` and its two helpers move unchanged. They read `descriptionsOf` over the same catalogue that MCP's `marks.ts` read. `Reads` moves to the client unchanged, apart from relative imports and the `randomUUID` declaration in `web.d.ts`.\n- `InstallOptions` has exactly four parts: `reader`, `admit`, `send` and `packageBytes`. The client imports nothing from `dap-git`.\n- MCP's mapping keeps its words, and its order matches the old code:\n  - `#admitTarget` can stop only with `unknown-tool`, so mapping any `Stop` from the hook to `unknown-tool` keeps the old result.\n  - The `send` port calls `#sendAct` with the snapshot that `admit` took, so originals at membership and hosted dispatch still apply. It wraps MCP's `Stop` in `SendStop`, and the client rethrows the cause unchanged.\n  - The read after acceptance gives `accepted-unread` on a `TransportError`, where `#afterAccepted` did the same.\n  - `#invalidate` still runs only after an accepted install.\n- The command line:\n  - `application-install-runtime.ts` builds `Custody` over the same `private/mcp-custody` file store and passes `custody.send` with no `admit`.\n  - The old command built `McpService` with no `originals` port, so it already used plain custody send. Only the client-side tool policy goes, which ruling 19a509a5 Q2 allows, and the scope still judges the install.\n  - `main.ts` imports `./mcp.ts` only for `dap mcp`.\n  - The note lists every changed line, old beside new. `docs/cli.md` quotes none of them.\n- `./install` is source-only:\n  - The client root does not import it.\n  - The release plan excludes it from the client's published exports and inputs.\n  - The command line is a private package, so no published package needs to resolve the subpath.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 2216316e is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 31 paths that the 31 artifacts cover, all at the head. `packages/mcp/src/reads.ts` is the source of a rename. The primary artifact is neither stale nor retired.\n- Cheap checks. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The commit-message check passes: 2 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean.\n- Tests, on my own clone of the head. `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 12 of 12, so the seven seals in the note equal what the seal functions compute. `scripts/public-release-modules.test.mjs` passes 5 of 5, and `scripts/active-source.test.mjs` passes 12 of 12. I ran no other tests.\n- Witnesses.\n  - The command-line witness runs the real `bin/dap.js` in a child process. It records every loaded module and finds none under `packages/mcp`, `@generalbusiness/dap-mcp` or `@modelcontextprotocol`.\n  - The control at 7ea170c9 recorded 526 modules, 51 of them under `packages/mcp`.\n  - In the evidence, the MCP word cases run at 7ea170c9 and at the head give equal output. That output equals `install-words-7ea170c9.json` byte for byte.\n- Evidence. All 159 files that the manifest lists match their SHA-256 values in `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence`. The gate at 18ebc428 wrote exit 0 and \"gate passed\", and its counts agree with END 9ab19928. Its tree equals the manifest's `checkpointTree`, and from 18ebc428 to the head only the note and the manifest change.\n- CI. GitHub reports Card run 43362876648 as a push event, attempt 1, completed and successful, at 18ebc428.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The client owns one install request and one installation read. Each caller supplies its own policy, its own send path and its own Git reader, and writes its own words. The command line and `dap mcp` share one custody directory and one declaration digest. A request that one of them keeps therefore settles from the other.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The trust setting is read again inside custody's build, and the publisher check stays before signing. The receipt and entry checks after acceptance are unchanged. The command line signs with its own key under custody, and the scope judges the install. The custody warning after an early refusal reads the store without taking a lock and writes nothing.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes for a later head:\n\n1. `applicationPackageBytes` in `service.ts` and `packageBytes` in `application-install-runtime.ts` are the same function. `@generalbusiness/dap-git/application` could export it once, and the client would still not depend on `dap-git`.\n2. `early` in the command-line runtime names the refusals that come after a send, so any new refusal counts as early by default. A field on the refusal type that says whether a request went would make that choice in one place.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing and deploys.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0555e4034a0955b035611ff92ce4edd0a1ada274","binding":"assigned","head":"1904c9458a3414dc1998cab6bb72ad3912f6a94b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dc5dd0af15214415c82d7fb2ce2d1f2598133cb6\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c67cd117b942566d06b34c7ea6d0c899d827b22f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fc038fd7df4146da30a1f0c9e37bbbb2cade6fb5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}